The overall of structure of the method incorporating the disentangled sessions is shown in Figure 3.

For the vanilla model using conversation $\mathcal{C}$ without any disentanglement, we use the LSTM, MLP and self attention as in Equation 22-26 to obtain its vector representation $v_{\mathcal{C}}^{\prime}$ . And then the matching score is calculated by the dot product between $v_{\mathcal{C}}^{\prime}$ and $v_{m}$ .

The whole model is trained to minimize the cross-entropy loss of both positive instances and negative instances.
